00:47:12,120 --> 00:47:13,800
specific foundational systems,

1730
00:47:14,060 --> 00:47:15,460
specifically something called

1731
00:47:15,460 --> 00:47:17,000
the calculus of constructions,

1732
00:47:17,180 --> 00:47:17,720
or COSI.

1733
00:47:18,120 --> 00:47:19,140
We touched on the edges

1734
00:47:19,140 --> 00:47:19,920
of this earlier

1735
00:47:19,920 --> 00:47:20,860
when you asked

1736
00:47:20,860 --> 00:47:22,600
why simple type systems fail.

1737
00:47:23,600 --> 00:47:24,900
The calculus of constructions

1738
00:47:24,900 --> 00:47:26,120
is a highly advanced

1739
00:47:26,120 --> 00:47:27,140
formal system

1740
00:47:27,140 --> 00:47:28,020
in pipe theory

1741
00:47:28,020 --> 00:47:29,200
that allows for

1742
00:47:29,200 --> 00:47:30,020
dependent types.

1743
00:47:30,420 --> 00:47:31,420
It allows types

1744
00:47:31,420 --> 00:47:32,900
to dynamically depend

1745
00:47:32,900 --> 00:47:34,460
on runtime values.

1746
00:47:34,920 --> 00:47:35,400
I want to use

1747
00:47:35,400 --> 00:47:36,600
that file reading example

1748
00:47:36,600 --> 00:47:37,760
again to make this concrete.

1749
00:47:37,920 --> 00:47:38,160
Perfect.

1750
00:47:38,400 --> 00:47:39,260
If you write a function

1751
00:47:39,260 --> 00:47:40,460
to read a file in Java,

1752
00:47:40,460 --> 00:47:42,060
a simple type system

1753
00:47:42,060 --> 00:47:42,920
says the output

1754
00:47:42,920 --> 00:47:43,480
of that function

1755
00:47:43,480 --> 00:47:44,100
is a string.

1756
00:47:44,480 --> 00:47:45,080
It just tells you

1757
00:47:45,080 --> 00:47:45,860
the shape of the data.

1758
00:47:46,260 --> 00:47:47,200
The compiler doesn't know

1759
00:47:47,200 --> 00:47:48,280
which specific file

1760
00:47:48,280 --> 00:47:49,400
produced the string.

1761
00:47:49,740 --> 00:47:50,340
In the calculus

1762
00:47:50,340 --> 00:47:51,340
of constructions,

1763
00:47:51,620 --> 00:47:52,460
the type of the output

1764
00:47:52,460 --> 00:47:53,560
can actually encapsulate

1765
00:47:53,560 --> 00:47:55,040
the specific runtime value

1766
00:47:55,040 --> 00:47:55,880
that generated it.

1767
00:47:56,420 --> 00:47:57,620
The type isn't just string.

1768
00:47:58,000 --> 00:47:59,340
The type is file contents

1769
00:47:59,340 --> 00:48:00,900
with a specific path attached.

1770
00:48:01,560 --> 00:48:03,060
The type dynamically morphs

1771
00:48:03,060 --> 00:48:03,980
depending on the specific

1772
00:48:03,980 --> 00:48:05,140
file path you feed it.

1773
00:48:05,260 --> 00:48:06,660
That feels incredibly powerful.

1774
00:48:07,060 --> 00:48:07,780
The type system

1775
00:48:07,780 --> 00:48:09,480
is aware of the actual data

1776
00:48:09,480 --> 00:48:10,600
flowing through the program.

1777
00:48:11,000 --> 00:48:11,360
It is.

1778
00:48:11,640 --> 00:48:11,940
Furthermore,

1779
00:48:12,300 --> 00:48:13,280
Kurian allows terms

1780
00:48:13,280 --> 00:48:14,340
to function as types,

1781
00:48:14,820 --> 00:48:15,560
blurring the line

1782
00:48:15,560 --> 00:48:16,780
between data and structure.

1783
00:48:17,420 --> 00:48:18,580
To prevent the mathematics

1784
00:48:18,580 --> 00:48:19,300
from collapsing

1785
00:48:19,300 --> 00:48:20,360
into paradoxes,

1786
00:48:20,560 --> 00:48:21,440
like Russell's paradox,

1787
00:48:22,000 --> 00:48:23,160
where a set contains

1788
00:48:23,160 --> 00:48:24,200
all sets that don't

1789
00:48:24,200 --> 00:48:25,000
contain themselves,

1790
00:48:25,500 --> 00:48:26,200
Kurki employs

1791
00:48:26,200 --> 00:48:28,020
a strict universe hierarchy.

1792
00:48:28,260 --> 00:48:29,120
I always think of

1793
00:48:29,120 --> 00:48:30,080
Russell's paradox

1794
00:48:30,080 --> 00:48:31,200
as a snake eating

1795
00:48:31,200 --> 00:48:32,000
its own tail

1796
00:48:32,000 --> 00:48:33,360
until the universe implodes.

1797
00:48:33,460 --> 00:48:33,800
Exactly.

1798
00:48:34,220 --> 00:48:35,060
To stop the snake

1799
00:48:35,060 --> 00:48:35,980
from eating itself,

1800
00:48:36,080 --> 00:48:37,300
Kurki separates logic

1801
00:48:37,300 --> 00:48:37,980
into layers.

1802
00:48:38,560 --> 00:48:40,340
Type 0, type 1, type 2

1803
00:48:40,340 --> 00:48:41,600
ascending infinitely.

1804
00:48:42,120 --> 00:48:42,880
A type at level 1

1805
00:48:42,880 --> 00:48:44,000
can only describe things

1806
00:48:44,000 --> 00:48:44,580
at level 0.

1807
00:48:45,160 --> 00:48:45,820
This hierarchy

1808
00:48:45,820 --> 00:48:46,860
acts as a mathematical

1809
00:48:46,860 --> 00:48:48,020
scaffolding to ensure

1810
00:48:48,020 --> 00:48:49,240
the system remains sound

1811
00:48:49,240 --> 00:48:50,620
and doesn't swallow itself

1812
00:48:50,620 --> 00:48:51,520
in a recursive loop

1813
00:48:51,520 --> 00:48:52,160
of definitions.

1814
00:48:52,600 --> 00:48:53,000
But then,

1815
00:48:53,100 --> 00:48:54,040
right after diving

1816
00:48:54,040 --> 00:48:55,640
into this massive type theory,

1817
00:48:55,840 --> 00:48:56,460
