1829
00:49:10,120 --> 00:49:10,720
to the architecture?

1830
00:49:11,000 --> 00:49:12,280
It circles back beautifully

1831
00:49:12,280 --> 00:49:13,400
to the note taxonomy

1832
00:49:13,400 --> 00:49:14,280
we discussed earlier.

1833
00:49:14,800 --> 00:49:15,720
Freckney views BNF

1834
00:49:15,720 --> 00:49:16,620
not just as syntax

1835
00:49:16,620 --> 00:49:17,840
but as the ultimate

1836
00:49:17,840 --> 00:49:19,140
generative refusal note.

1837
00:49:19,380 --> 00:49:20,240
How does grammar

1838
00:49:20,240 --> 00:49:21,460
act as a refusal note?

1839
00:49:21,900 --> 00:49:22,740
A BNF grammar

1840
00:49:22,740 --> 00:49:23,920
is a set of rules

1841
00:49:23,920 --> 00:49:24,760
that specifies

1842
00:49:24,760 --> 00:49:26,040
exactly what strings

1843
00:49:26,040 --> 00:49:26,560
of characters

1844
00:49:26,560 --> 00:49:27,880
are mathematically valid

1845
00:49:27,880 --> 00:49:28,800
in a given language

1846
00:49:28,800 --> 00:49:30,100
and by definition,

1847
00:49:30,620 --> 00:49:31,920
it rigorously refuses

1848
00:49:31,920 --> 00:49:33,200
all other combinations.

1849
00:49:33,520 --> 00:49:34,960
It is pure specification.

1850
00:49:34,960 --> 00:49:36,640
A physical circuit diagram

1851
00:49:36,640 --> 00:49:37,800
is severely limited

1852
00:49:37,800 --> 00:49:38,900
because it is

1853
00:49:38,900 --> 00:49:40,180
inextricably tied

1854
00:49:40,180 --> 00:49:41,480
to the physical topology

1855
00:49:41,480 --> 00:49:42,580
of copper wires

1856
00:49:42,580 --> 00:49:43,520
and silicon gates.

1857
00:49:43,780 --> 00:49:44,520
A C program

1858
00:49:44,520 --> 00:49:45,800
is tied to the quirks

1859
00:49:45,800 --> 00:49:47,020
of a specific compiler

1860
00:49:47,020 --> 00:49:47,580
architecture

1861
00:49:47,580 --> 00:49:49,380
and the CPU instruction set

1862
00:49:49,380 --> 00:49:51,040
but BNF operates

1863
00:49:51,040 --> 00:49:52,280
at a level of abstraction

1864
00:49:52,280 --> 00:49:53,460
completely unmoored

1865
00:49:53,460 --> 00:49:54,060
from hardware.

1866
00:49:54,260 --> 00:49:55,560
It's the pure idea

1867
00:49:55,560 --> 00:49:56,120
of the language.

1868
00:49:56,220 --> 00:49:56,540
Yes.

1869
00:49:56,880 --> 00:49:57,820
It is human readable,

1870
00:49:58,240 --> 00:49:59,380
it is machine parsable,

1871
00:49:59,660 --> 00:50:00,400
and it serves

1872
00:50:00,400 --> 00:50:01,940
as a mathematical firewall

1873
00:50:01,940 --> 00:50:03,580
against implementation bias.

1874
00:50:03,580 --> 00:50:04,740
When you write

1875
00:50:04,740 --> 00:50:05,560
a system's rules

1876
00:50:05,560 --> 00:50:06,120
in BNF,

1877
00:50:06,280 --> 00:50:06,820
you are creating

1878
00:50:06,820 --> 00:50:07,740
a generative artifact

1879
00:50:07,740 --> 00:50:08,640
that opens up

1880
00:50:08,640 --> 00:50:09,380
new possibilities,

1881
00:50:09,880 --> 00:50:10,460
you can generate

1882
00:50:10,460 --> 00:50:11,840
infinite valid programs

1883
00:50:11,840 --> 00:50:13,000
while simultaneously

1884
00:50:13,000 --> 00:50:14,620
erecting an impenetrable

1885
00:50:14,620 --> 00:50:15,580
wall of refusal

1886
00:50:15,580 --> 00:50:17,180
against invalid structures.

1887
00:50:17,520 --> 00:50:18,240
And as if that

1888
00:50:18,240 --> 00:50:19,080
wasn't deep enough,

1889
00:50:19,380 --> 00:50:20,080
the source drops

1890
00:50:20,080 --> 00:50:21,440
